---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="About Yan Zeng and current academic interests.">
  <div class="page">
    <header class="page-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>About Yan Zeng</h1>
      <p>
        Philosophy, AI ethics, trust, and the social structure of human-AI
        dependence.
      </p>
    </header>

    <article class="prose">
      <p>
        Yan Zeng is a PhD student in philosophy at the University of California,
        Irvine. His current work examines epistemology, AI ethics, trust, and the
        structure of human-AI dependence.
      </p>
      <p>
        A central theme of this work is how technical systems redistribute
        responsibility. In AI-mediated practices, people are often described as
        the final human authority, but they may not actually have the expertise,
        time, or institutional power needed to bear that responsibility fairly.
      </p>
      <p>
        This site is a public research notebook for reviewed notes, essays, and
        academic materials. AI may help generate drafts, but nothing is published
        without human review.
      </p>

      <h2>Research Areas</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Epistemology and social epistemology.</li>
        <li>Trust, reliance, and dependence in human-AI systems.</li>
        <li>AI ethics, role-burden allocation, and institutional responsibility.</li>
        <li>Technology, deskilling, and the transformation of social practices.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Public Writing</h2>
      <p>
        The writing here is intentionally selective. It is meant to turn ongoing
        philosophical work into durable public notes while keeping drafts,
        private records, and raw conversations out of the published site.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
